target
artifacts
coverage

# Fuzz corpora are GENERATED data — libFuzzer writes every newly-discovered unit
# into the corpus directory — so they stay out of the repo by default.
corpus/*

# EXCEPTION (Phase 115-09, SCHM-01): the hand-written SEED corpus for
# `fuzz_schema_draft_pin`. Its input format is length-prefixed precisely so seeds
# can be written by hand and committed; without them the target overwhelmingly
# explores inputs where neither half parses as JSON and degenerates into a
# JSON-parser fuzz that never reaches schema COMPILATION (threat T-115-41).
# Replaying the committed seeds is an acceptance criterion of `115-09-PLAN.md`.
#
# Only the README and the numbered seed files are tracked; anything else in that
# directory is a unit libFuzzer discovered at runtime and stays ignored, so a
# local fuzzing session never dirties the working tree.
!corpus/fuzz_schema_draft_pin/
corpus/fuzz_schema_draft_pin/*
!corpus/fuzz_schema_draft_pin/README.md
!corpus/fuzz_schema_draft_pin/[0-9][0-9]_*

# EXCEPTION (Phase 116-08, AUTH-01/AUTH-03): the hand-written SEED corpus for
# `oauth_authorization_response`. The accept path requires a callback query whose
# `state` reproduces a fixed 15-byte token EXACTLY, so random bytes essentially
# never reach it and the target degenerates into a no-panic check that can never
# evaluate its Ok-side invariants (threat T-116-29).
#
# MEASURED, not reasoned: with four deliberate breaks applied to
# `src/shared/oauth_validation.rs` at once, a 200000-run campaign from an EMPTY
# corpus found ZERO of them, while six of these seeds crash the same binary
# immediately. The seeds ARE the fence.
#
# Only the README and the `seed_*` files are tracked; anything else in that
# directory is a unit libFuzzer discovered at runtime and stays ignored, so a
# local fuzzing session never dirties the working tree.
!corpus/oauth_authorization_response/
corpus/oauth_authorization_response/*
!corpus/oauth_authorization_response/README.md
!corpus/oauth_authorization_response/seed_*

# EXCEPTION (Phase 116-08, AUTH-02/AUTH-03): the hand-written SEED corpus for
# `oauth_credential_and_dcr`. The credential document, the DCR response and the
# `redirect_uris` vector are all STRUCTURED inputs — a schema-1 document needs a
# `schema_version`, an `entries` object and a per-entry `access_token` and
# `client_id` before it parses at all — so random bytes degenerate into a JSON
# tokenizer fuzz that never reaches the migration, the round trip or the
# `application_type` accessor.
#
# MEASURED, not reasoned: with five deliberate breaks applied across
# `credential_store.rs`, `oauth_validation.rs` and `provider.rs` at once, a
# 200000-run campaign from an EMPTY corpus found ZERO of them, while these seeds
# caught all five with a clean per-seed partition.
#
# Only the README and the `seed_*` files are tracked.
!corpus/oauth_credential_and_dcr/
corpus/oauth_credential_and_dcr/*
!corpus/oauth_credential_and_dcr/README.md
!corpus/oauth_credential_and_dcr/seed_*

# EXCEPTION (Phase 128-10, SC-7 / T-128-47): the hand-written SEED corpus for
# `fuzz_input_schema_enforcement`. Its input format is length-prefixed precisely
# so seeds can be written by hand and committed — without them the target
# overwhelmingly explores inputs where neither document parses as JSON and
# degenerates into a JSON-parser fuzz that never reaches validation, the same
# degeneracy `fuzz_schema_draft_pin` records above.
#
# Each seed additionally chooses the target's BOUNDED SCHEMA PROJECTION through
# the keywords its own schema document declares (`additionalProperties`,
# `maxLength`, `pattern`, `required`, `patternProperties`, `enum`, `format`,
# array `items`), so the corpus covers every arm of the refusal renderer rather
# than only the JSON-parse boundary. The two PHI-shaped-key seeds (`01`, `05`) are
# the `safe_pointer` redaction cases; `09` is the uncompilable-declared-pattern
# case, whose refusal must stay detail-free.
#
# MEASURED, not reasoned: the un-ignore is necessary. `git check-ignore -v
# fuzz/corpus/fuzz_input_schema_enforcement` matched `fuzz/.gitignore:7`
# (`corpus/*`) before these four lines existed, so the seeds this plan requires
# would have been silently untracked — a corpus the repository cannot carry is not
# a corpus.
#
# Only the README and the numbered seed files are tracked; anything else in that
# directory is a unit libFuzzer discovered at runtime and stays ignored, so a
# local fuzzing session never dirties the working tree.
!corpus/fuzz_input_schema_enforcement/
corpus/fuzz_input_schema_enforcement/*
!corpus/fuzz_input_schema_enforcement/README.md
!corpus/fuzz_input_schema_enforcement/[0-9][0-9]_*

# EXCEPTION (Phase 128-10, T-128-48): the hand-written SEED corpus for
# `fuzz_placeholder_pattern_redos`. Same length-prefix argument as above, plus one
# specific to this target: the four classic catastrophic-backtracking shapes
# (`(a+)+`, `(a|aa)+`, `([0-9]+)*`, `((a)*)*`) are vanishingly unlikely to be
# discovered from random bytes, and they are precisely what RESEARCH assumption A2
# is about. A LOOK for A2 that cannot reach a nested quantifier is not a look.
#
# `05` is the benign ACCEPT control (a real version pattern that matches), `06` is
# the D-10 ordering control (a permissive `^.*$` must not widen the character
# floor), and `08` is the uncompilable-pattern case.
#
# Only the README and the numbered seed files are tracked.
!corpus/fuzz_placeholder_pattern_redos/
corpus/fuzz_placeholder_pattern_redos/*
!corpus/fuzz_placeholder_pattern_redos/README.md
!corpus/fuzz_placeholder_pattern_redos/[0-9][0-9]_*
